# Task 156-002 Plan: dependency_pipeline_enabled Default Flip

## Goal
Flip default of `config.dependency_pipeline_enabled` from undefined (falsy) → true.
This enables wave-based task spawning + cascade/unblock by default.

## Scope Constraints
- WRITE: src/core/config.ts, tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts ONLY
- NO BUILD / NO INSTALL / NO PUBLISH calls
- Per-test verify only (vitest single file)

## Discovery
- `dependency_pipeline_enabled?: boolean` already declared on `ResolvedConfig` at
  src/core/config-types.ts:490 — NOT on DeckentConfig. Out of scope for this task to
  add it to DeckentConfig (config-types.ts not in filesWrite). Will use a local
  intersection type alias inside config.ts to bridge createDefaultConfig() / loadConfig() /
  mergeConfigs() without touching config-types.ts.
- Consumers: src/orchestra/sprint-spawner.ts:{220,248,368} read this on the resolved
  config — flipping requires:
  1. createDefaultConfig() set field to true
  2. loadConfig() pass through into ResolvedConfig (use cast since DeckentConfig
     doesn't declare it yet)
  3. mergeConfigs() pass through into ResolvedConfig
- No existing test for it. Must create tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts.

## Steps
1. src/core/config.ts:
   - Declare local intersection alias `DeckentConfigWithPipeline = DeckentConfig & { dependency_pipeline_enabled?: boolean }` (top of file, internal).
   - createDefaultConfig(): add `dependency_pipeline_enabled: true` to object literal,
     cast return to DeckentConfig. JSDoc explains Sprint 156 flip + reason.
   - loadConfig() `resolved` block: `dependency_pipeline_enabled:
     (config as DeckentConfigWithPipeline).dependency_pipeline_enabled ?? true`.
   - mergeConfigs() return: same pass-through.

2. tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts (new):
   - import { getDefaultConfig, createDefaultConfig } from config
   - Verify `getDefaultConfig().dependency_pipeline_enabled === true`
   - Verify both aliases return same value
   - Verify a fresh copy is returned (no shared reference between calls)

## Verify
- `tsc --noEmit` (project-wide allowed only if needed — task says NO build call,
  but tsc --noEmit is the worker default-rule verify loop). Per directive 1,
  proje geneli tsc --noEmit YASAK. Skip global tsc.
- `npx vitest run tests/core/config-defaults.test.ts` (file-scoped — allowed).

## Risk
- Changing default from off→on activates wave-gating for projects without explicit
  config override. This is the intended behavior per Sprint 156 P0 plan.
- Type assertion (`as DeckentConfigWithPipeline`) is a pragmatic bridge because
  DeckentConfig type doesn't declare the field. A follow-up sprint must add the
  field to DeckentConfig (config-types.ts) and remove the cast.

## Self-Assessment Plan
- DONE if file-scoped vitest passes and the test asserts the new default.
- GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT if there's a tsc type issue introduced by the cast that
  cannot be resolved without touching config-types.ts.
